health!" That afternoon, Olivia presented her

33
00:01:49.282 --> 00:01:53.430
report. She held up a poster with a big yellow

34
00:01:53.431 --> 00:01:57.439
sun. "You may think a tan looks good," she

35
00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.687
said. "But too much sun can cause burns now—and skin cancer

36
00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:05.436
later. So use

37
00:02:05.437 --> 00:02:07.834
sunscreen." Olivia held up another

38
00:02:07.835 --> 00:02:12.234
poster. "In Hawaii they have bugs called

39
00:02:12.235 --> 00:02:17.712
centipedes. They can grow to be thirty centimeters long, and they

40
00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:22.891
sting. This black bug isn’t a centipede. It’s a

41
00:02:22.892 --> 00:02:26.430
tick." Katie smiled from ear to

42
00:02:26.431 --> 00:02:33.635
ear. "If you’ve been walking in tall grass," said Olivia, "check for ticks when you go

43
00:02:33.636 --> 00:02:36.411
inside." Olivia held up her last

44
00:02:36.412 --> 00:02:41.688
poster. "Poison ivy," she

45
00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:47.613
said. "If you see a plant like this—with three leaves—stay

46
