51
00:03:05.863 --> 00:03:07.608
Just like my necklace!

52
00:03:07.609 --> 00:03:10.047
Go ahead and try some."

53
00:03:10.048 --> 00:03:14.310
"Very nice report," said Ms. Barrow.

54
00:03:14.311 --> 00:03:16.618
Carlos was next.

55
00:03:16.619 --> 00:03:23.913
"If you didn’t have ears," said Carlos, "you couldn’t hear sirens, trains, or even tornadoes."

56
00:03:23.914 --> 00:03:29.414
"We wouldn’t be able to hear you!" said Katie.

57
00:03:29.415 --> 00:03:31.621
"So you must protect your ears."

58
00:03:31.622 --> 00:03:34.252
Carlos looked at his note card.

59
00:03:34.253 --> 00:03:37.404
"Loud sounds can harm your ears.

60
00:03:37.405 --> 00:03:42.705
If other people can hear music from your earphones, the music is too loud."

61
00:03:42.706 --> 00:03:46.216
Carlos looked at his note card again.

62
00:03:46.217 --> 00:03:48.805
"Don’t put anything pointy in your ears.

63
00:03:48.806 --> 00:03:52.632
In fact, don’t put anything in your ears.

64
00:03:52.633 --> 00:03:56.981
That’s all," he said and returned to his desk.

65
00:03:56.982 --> 00:04:02.058
"Good report," whispered Katie. "Short and sweet."

66
00:04:02.059 --> 00:04:06.122
Luke’s report on healthy eating was the last one of the day.

67
00:04:06.123 --> 00:04:09.954
He was serving snacks!

68
00:04:09.955 --> 00:04:14.815
"Food is like gasoline for our bodies!" said Luke.

69
00:04:14.816 --> 00:04:17.443
"We can’t run without it."

70
00:04:17.444 --> 00:04:22.015
He unrolled a big poster and pinned it to the whiteboard.

71
00:04:22.016 --> 00:04:24.005
"This is a food pyramid.

72
00:04:24.006 --> 00:04:28.398
And these are snacks prepared by my mom at Fried Pie Heaven.

73
00:04:28.399 --> 00:04:31.531
They include all the food groups in the pyramid.

74
00:04:31.532 --> 00:04:37.379
Fruits, vegetables, grains, dairy, and nuts!"

75
00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.445
"Where are the fried pies?" asked Larry.

76
00:04:41.446 --> 00:04:46.872
Luke sighed. "I’ve got bad news," he said.

77
00:04:46.873 --> 00:04:50.463
"Fried pies are not on the pyramid."

78
00:04:50.464 --> 00:04:54.607
"WHAT?" cried the fourth graders.

79
00:04:54.608 --> 00:04:56.981
"They have too much fat and sugar.

80
00:04:56.982 --> 00:04:59.594
We shouldn’t eat them very often.

81
00:04:59.595 --> 00:05:04.629
That’s why my mom makes sure there are healthy foods on the menu too."

82
00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:07.366
"Dig in!" said Luke.

83
00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:13.133
While the fourth graders ate, Katie sneaked up behind Luke and Carlos.

84
00:05:13.134 --> 00:05:17.123
"Hi, guys!" she said with a big grin.

85
00:05:17.124 --> 00:05:20.002
"Is tonight okay for square-dance practice?

86
00:05:20.003 --> 00:05:26.010
My presentation is tomorrow!"

